  "title": "Erdős Problem #976",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $f\\in \\mathbb{Z}[x]$ be an irreducible polynomial of degree $d\\geq 2$. Let $F_f(n)$ be maximal such that there exists $1\\leq m\\leq n$ with $f(m)$ is divisible by a prime $\\geq F_f(n)$. Equivalently, $F_f(n)$ is the greatest prime divisor of $ \\prod_{1\\leq m\\leq n}f(m). $ Estimate $F_f(n)$. In particular, is it true that $F_f(n)\\gg n^{1+c}$ for some constant $c>0$? Or even $\\gg n^d$?",
